- op: discuss  # 4fae
  at: '2026-10-13T00:01:48Z'  # 4fae
  by: agent  # 4fae
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4fae
  clock: 3  # 4fae
  nonce: 4fae  # 4fae
  message: "Fixed in PR #1562 (merge 907d2f25d3). Root cause: confirmed — each of the four analyzers kept a per-file set of seen names (ocaml/agda/lean add_symbol seen_names; wolfram the same), so the first symbol of a name won and later same-name declarations were silently dropped. Fix: removed the name dedup; every declaration is emitted with its scope chain (ocaml/agda/lean nested module/namespace -> name A.run; agda fields Pair.fst, constructors bare with the data type in the chain; wolfram each definition, read from the LHS text since the grammar cannot parse blank patterns, with pattern heads/literals as typed discriminants) and a producer stable_id via declared_arity_stable_id. Evidence (dev 907d2f25d3): hypergumbo run on a probe dir with the filed shapes -> ocaml A.run line 2 sha256:43ec7113f8566247, B.run line 5 sha256:15011675e44f9104, top-level run line 7 sha256:c45f49d274e452c5 and run line 8 sha256:a26c9ab9038603be (shadowing redefinition, both present); agda A.run line 8 sha256:a8969a68da401f61, B.run line 12 sha256:eb69603d7f35d3a8, Pair.fst line 17 sha256:94885299e9900c2e, Box.fst line 21 sha256:d6145edf70580a84; lean A.run line 2 sha256:68b24d8009296b4e, B.run line 5 sha256:9e21dab89bcf529c; wolfram run line 1 sha256:26b9a3f3c8a9cadc, run line 2 sha256:5a80b719da5cac5a, helper line 3 sha256:5b7e9b62abb5f79d (helper[] was also missing before). Each checked per symbol, all non-null and distinct. Caveat seen while probing: tree-sitter-agda mis-parses a data type with a single constructor (ERROR node swallows the next module), unrelated to this fix; type/module table kinds keep bare names and are told apart by the occurrence split (qualifying them is a scheme-bump change)."  # 4fae
